Bugfix: Park inactive file list views so ids stay unique in the document

The files view loads seven list templates into the same document - files,
favorites, incoming, outgoing and link shares, trash and tags. Only one is
visible at a time, but all of them were present in the DOM and each carried
the same set of ids. Fourteen ids were therefore assigned more than once,
affecting 68 elements.

Duplicate ids break the association created by label[for] and
aria-labelledby, because assistive technology only evaluates the first
element carrying an id. They are also a robustness risk outside
accessibility, because the application reads several of these ids directly
and always receives the first occurrence.

Inactive views are now kept inside inert <template> elements and are only
placed into the document while they are active, so exactly one set of list
ids exists at any time.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 4.1.1
